FULL SCENIC CHAPEL_C SOURCE AND PROVENANCE KIT

Untouched source: native_floor.png, 1536x1024 RGB. Exact generation prompt, available style block and generation metadata are included. Requested generation-model names are prompt intent, not verified backend identifiers. The approved condensed style is recorded in the exact prompt; supplied approved viewport references are included under references. Source metadata preserves the requested generation scale; review_views_metadata.json records the adopted 64px-source hero scale after visual review. Generation geometry/camera is not mathematically validated.

The separate AI output is 6144x4096 from genuine 4x Real-ESRGAN anime 6B inference. The 3072x2048 option is that result reduced with Pillow Lanczos, not a native 2x model. Upscaling does not restore unavailable ground-truth detail.
One continuous source is processed as 70 computational batches: 160px cores, 32px context, 16px additional reflected processing border; discard context without blending. Each batch uses a fresh process, and the full canvas is assembled afterward. This is not artistic stitching. 2 threads requested after model loading; NCNN Winograd convolutions retain the load-time 4-thread setting. OMP_NUM_THREADS=2 was also set.
Completed wall time: 188.879 seconds. Peak child RSS: 3316108 KiB. Seam metrics are in metrics/seam_metrics.json; checks compare actual output pixels with independent untiled inference, not unavailable high-resolution ground truth.
Hero contexts use the original approved RGBA hero, resized conventionally to 160px visible height. Recommended art scale is a 64px hero equivalent in the source, or 256px in the raw AI4x asset. For these familiar 160px-hero views, the raw AI scene is reduced by 0.625 to 3840x2560 (2.5x native); each display crop is 1536x1024, corresponding to 614.4x409.6 source pixels. This is a display/world-scale recommendation, not a claim of exact 4x ground extent. Hero/shadow overlays exist only in review images, never in the floor. Display crop boxes and foot placements are recorded in review_config.json; exact source-equivalent crop boxes, display scale and conversion are in review_views_metadata.json. No engine test was performed.

BAKED SCENERY CAVEATS
Scenery throughout the scene is intentionally baked into the flat image. The image alone does not provide collision, walkability, depth sorting or occlusion masks. A character cannot automatically pass behind a pillar, tree or tomb merely because it is painted here. Gameplay would require separate collision geometry and front-occlusion layers/masks or separated props. Hero contexts are composited scale illustrations, not engine integration, pathfinding or camera validation.

